  "readmeFile": "NugetREADME.md",
  "releaseNotes": "DicomImage.Bitmap Prevent reassigning exceptions by rethrowing so original exception can be viewed.\nEOT tags are removed when transcoding on a Write, if same-syntax Write then EOT tags are kept and an Empty BOT is created.\nSKOpenGL incorrect matrix multiplication ordering causing pixel shifts fix.\nWhen pixel data > 4294967296 bytes the BOT is made empty (for all BasicOffsetTableHandling options).\nif SeekableBotHandling Seek option is selected and data is > 4294967296 then BOT is made empty and pixel data is shifted to remove that pre-allocated BOT length space.\nAdded a new WriteBehaviour option, SequentialFrameProcessing, which processes frames sequentially rather than in parallel during encoding, reducing memory consumption at the expense of encoding speed.\nBOT mode selection fix between WriteBehaviour.SeekableBotHandling and WriteBehaviour.NonSeekableBotHandling when the stream is seek able (was only considering FileStreams).\nAvoid double scale-down with Zoom and resLevel (J2K output size is down double what's requested).\nJpegXL support added into DicomObjects (libjxl).\nPadding byte when odd fragment stream length.\nOptimised JPEG encoding to write only the quantization tables required by the image, omitting unused chrominance quantization tables for monochrome images (Jpeg XL Recompression will throw exception if there are unused quantization tables).\nOmit BOT if Video TS, each fragment is added to a single frame.\nPublic API change - FixPossibleExplictTagsWithinImplicitSequence renamed to FixPossibleExplicitTagsWithinImplicitSequence (spelling mistake)\nOnly throw OpenGL is unavailable exception when its actually unavailable and not just when a render fails.\nAdded DicomGlobal.IsOpenGLAvailable() to check whether OpenGL can be initialized on the machine.\nDicomDataSet.GetMinAndMax fix overwriting reslevel with Full.\nDicomImage.Bitmap fix to prevent creating a subset of the bitmap that was outside the image dimensions.\nAdded DicomDataSet.GetNativeFrame method for \"stored\" pixel data.\nJ2K codec, check if SIZ marker is defined correctly.\nResolution level is considered when windowing tags are missing and windowing values are calculated from the pixel data, the pixels histogram account for the resolution level when retrieving from cache.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": false,
  "verbatimVersion": "10.0.8.4-preview",
